      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © AULA MEDICA EDICIONES 2013. Published by AULA MEDICA. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Vitamin A deficiency may occur after malabsorptive bariatric surgery. However, it rarely entails important functionally limiting symptoms. We present the case of a woman who underwent bariatric surgery and developed ocular dryness, xeroderma and hearing loss due to severe vitamin A deficiency. We illustrate an outstanding and exceptional case of the consequences of an excessive and uncontrolled malabsorption."
      },
